{% comment %}
HappyFox — renders a glanceable help-desk dashboard from the serverless aggregator
(serverless.js). That `run(input)` returns an ordered `cards` array of
{ key, label, value, scope, name } for the user-selected metrics, plus `updated`
(ISO-8601 UTC) and `error`. Because it's a single data source, those keys arrive as
top-level merge variables, so the four size files pass `cards`, `updated`, and `error`
straight through.

Layout model: one user-chosen HERO (big number) leads, then the remaining metrics split by scope
into ME (`my_*`) and ALL (`all_*`). full, half-horizontal and quadrant use `scope_group`, a Me/All
header over a Liquid-capped card row. half-vertical uses `metric_rows` when both scopes show and
`scope_grid` when one does, sizing everything from the row count so the body fills the slot.
`card.name` is the scope-stripped label ("Open" instead of "My Open") so the header carries the
scope. The hero is the card matching the `hero` custom field, else the first card. The four size
files are thin {% raw %}{% render 'main', ... %}{% endraw %} wrappers that pass a `layout_size`.
{% endcomment %}

{% comment %} ---- one stat: a value over its (optionally scope-stripped) label ---- {% endcomment %}
{% template card %}
<div class="item">
  <div class="meta"></div>
  <div class="content">
    <span class="value {{ value_size | default: 'value--small' }} value--tnums"{% if card.value != nil %} data-value-format="true" data-fit-value="true"{% endif %}>{{ card.value | default: '—' }}</span>
    <span class="label {{ label_size | default: 'label--small' }}" data-clamp="2">{{ label_text | default: card.label }}</span>
  </div>
</div>
{% endtemplate %}

{% comment %} ---- title bar: inline HappyFox mark, instance name, last-updated time ---- {% endcomment %}
{% template title_bar %}
<div class="title_bar">
  <svg class="image" viewBox="0 0 18.979 18.835" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg">
    <g transform="translate(0 -.56641)" clip-path="url(#hf_clip0)">
      <g clip-path="url(#hf_clip1)" fill="#ff5a00">
        <path d="m2.5832 8.0872c0.40387 0 0.80012-0.1143 1.143-0.33275l4.1276-2.6188-5.7964-4.2241c-0.856-0.62486-2.0574-0.0127-2.0574 1.044v4.435l1.077 1.0719c0.40387 0.40133 0.93728 0.62232 1.5088 0.62232z"/>
        <path d="m0.45213 12.27 5.931 5.0928 2.0117 1.7273c0.46991 0.4038 1.1583 0.4165 1.6434 0.033l8.4483-6.6626c0.3099-0.2464 0.4927-0.6198 0.4927-1.016v-9.5811c0-1.0389-1.1658-1.6561-2.0244-1.0694l-7.7776 5.3087-4.6356 2.9414c-0.60199 0.38355-1.2827 0.56897-1.9584 0.56897-0.94236 0-1.8771-0.36323-2.5832-1.0668v2.7432c0 0.3785 0.1651 0.7367 0.45213 0.9805z"/>
      </g>
    </g>
    <defs>
      <clipPath id="hf_clip0"><rect width="105.15" height="20" fill="#fff"/></clipPath>
      <clipPath id="hf_clip1"><rect transform="translate(0 .56641)" width="18.979" height="18.835" fill="#fff"/></clipPath>
    </defs>
  </svg>
  {% if layout_size != 'quadrant' %}
  {%- comment -%} A portrait-mounted half-vertical is too narrow for the name beside the time. {%- endcomment -%}
  <span class="title{% if layout_size == 'half-vertical' %} portrait:hidden{% endif %}">{{ trmnl.plugin_settings.instance_name | default: 'HappyFox' }}</span>
  {% endif %}
  {% if updated %}
  <span class="instance">Updated <span data-dt="{{ updated | date: '%s' }}" data-dt-style="time"></span></span>
  {% endif %}
</div>
{% endtemplate %}

{% comment %}
---- one scope group (full / half-horizontal / quadrant — the static-cap sizes): a ME/ALL header
over the scope's non-hero cards, capped at `item_limit` with a hand-rendered "+N more" tail.
`total_count` is the scope's non-hero card count (precomputed in `main`). `inner_class` is the card
container — a `grid grid--cols-N` so rows align column-to-column. Everything in the scope chain
carries `self--stretch` — the per-size middle container, the scope_group root, and the inner card
grid — because each level is a `flex--col` (`align-items:center`), which otherwise shrinks + centers
a short grid to its content width. The header `self--start` keeps it left. Capping is explicit
Liquid, not the framework overflow JS.
{% endcomment %}
{% template scope_group %}
<div class="flex flex--col gap--small self--stretch">
  <span class="label label--small self--start">{{ heading }}</span>
  <div class="{{ inner_class | default: 'flex flex--col gap--small' }} self--stretch">
    {% assign shown = 0 %}
    {% for card in scope_cards %}{% unless card.key == hero_key %}{% if shown < item_limit %}
    {% render 'card', card: card, label_text: card.name, value_size: value_size, label_size: label_size %}
    {% assign shown = shown | plus: 1 %}
    {% endif %}{% endunless %}{% endfor %}
    {% assign hidden = total_count | minus: shown %}
    {% if hidden > 0 %}
    <span class="label label--small self--center no-shrink">+{{ hidden }} more</span>
    {% endif %}
  </div>
</div>
{% endtemplate %}

{% comment %}
---- half-vertical body, both scopes: a Me | All header over one grid row per metric type, so a
metric's two counts sit side by side. A missing or hero cell is an empty placeholder. Past six rows,
OG shows five plus a "+N more" line, since the overflow engine's budget runs about 20px long there
and clips its own counter. TRMNL X fits all eight possible rows. Capped cells sit in a
`hidden lg:block` wrapper because `lg:flex` on the `.item` would also widen its internal gap. The
grid keeps the slot height, so its rows stretch to fill it. The overflow engine stays as a fallback
for other screens. ----
{% endcomment %}
{% template metric_rows %}
<div class="flex flex--col gap--small stretch">
  <div class="grid grid--cols-2">
    <span class="label label--small">Me</span>
    <span class="label label--small">All</span>
  </div>
  {% assign scopes = 'my,all' | split: ',' %}
  {% assign capped = 0 %}
  <div class="grid grid--cols-2 stretch {{ grid_gap }}" data-overflow="true" data-overflow-max-height="auto" data-overflow-counter="true">
    {% for t in types %}
    {% assign cap = false %}{% if types.size > 6 and forloop.index > 5 %}{% assign cap = true %}{% endif %}
    {% for scope in scopes %}
    {% assign key = scope | append: '_' | append: t %}
    {% assign c = cards | where: 'key', key | first %}
    {% if cap %}<div class="hidden lg:block">{% endif %}
    {% if c and c.key != hero_key %}
    {% render 'card', card: c, label_text: c.name, value_size: value_size, label_size: label_size %}
    {% if cap %}{% assign capped = capped | plus: 1 %}{% endif %}
    {% else %}
    <div></div>
    {% endif %}
    {% if cap %}</div>{% endif %}
    {% endfor %}
    {% endfor %}
  </div>
  {% if capped > 0 %}<span class="label label--small lg:hidden">+{{ capped }} more</span>{% endif %}
</div>
{% endtemplate %}

{% comment %}
---- half-vertical body, one scope: a header over the scope's non-hero cards in two columns. At
most seven cards (four rows), which fits on every screen. ----
{% endcomment %}
{% template scope_grid %}
<div class="flex flex--col gap--small stretch">
  <span class="label label--small self--start">{{ heading }}</span>
  <div class="grid grid--cols-2 stretch {{ grid_gap }}" data-overflow="true" data-overflow-max-height="auto" data-overflow-counter="true">
    {% for card in scope_cards %}{% unless card.key == hero_key %}
    {% render 'card', card: card, label_text: card.name, value_size: value_size, label_size: label_size %}
    {% endunless %}{% endfor %}
  </div>
</div>
{% endtemplate %}

{% template main %}
{% comment %} 12/24-hour: force from the timemode custom field, else let the locale decide {% endcomment %}
{% if trmnl.plugin_settings.custom_fields_values.timemode == '24_hour' %}
{% assign hour12 = 'false' %}
{% else %}
{% assign hour12 = 'true' %}
{% endif %}

{% if error != blank or cards == blank %}
{%- comment -%} Empty / error state {%- endcomment -%}
<div class="layout layout--center">
  <span class="label lg:label--large text--center" data-clamp="3">{{ error | default: 'No HappyFox Data' }}</span>
</div>

{% else %}
{% comment %} Resolve the hero: the card matching the `hero` field, else the first card. {% endcomment %}
{% assign hero = cards[0] %}
{% assign hero_pick = trmnl.plugin_settings.custom_fields_values.hero %}
{% if hero_pick %}
{% assign hero_match = cards | where: 'key', hero_pick %}
{% if hero_match.size > 0 %}{% assign hero = hero_match[0] %}{% endif %}
{% endif %}
{% assign hero_key = hero.key %}

{% comment %} Split the supporting cards by scope (hero excluded at render time). {% endcomment %}
{% assign my_cards = cards | where: 'scope', 'my' %}
{% assign all_cards = cards | where: 'scope', 'all' %}
{% assign my_extra = 0 %}{% if hero.scope == 'my' %}{% assign my_extra = 1 %}{% endif %}
{% assign all_extra = 0 %}{% if hero.scope == 'all' %}{% assign all_extra = 1 %}{% endif %}
{% assign my_count = my_cards.size | minus: my_extra %}
{% assign all_count = all_cards.size | minus: all_extra %}

{% case layout_size %}

{% comment %} ================= FULL (800x480) ================= {% endcomment %}
{% when 'full' %}
<div class="layout layout--col">
  <div class="grid">
    {% render 'card', card: hero, value_size: 'value--xxxlarge lg:value--giga', label_size: 'label--large' %}
  </div>
  {% if my_count > 0 or all_count > 0 %}
  <div class="divider"></div>
  <div class="flex flex--col gap--space-between grow self--stretch">
    {% if my_count > 0 %}
    {% render 'scope_group', heading: 'Me', scope_cards: my_cards, hero_key: hero_key, total_count: my_count, item_limit: 5, inner_class: 'grid grid--cols-6', value_size: 'value--large lg:value--xlarge', label_size: 'label--small lg:label--base' %}
    {% endif %}
    {% if my_count > 0 and all_count > 0 %}
    <div class="divider"></div>
    {% endif %}
    {% if all_count > 0 %}
    {% render 'scope_group', heading: 'All', scope_cards: all_cards, hero_key: hero_key, total_count: all_count, item_limit: 5, inner_class: 'grid grid--cols-6', value_size: 'value--large lg:value--xlarge', label_size: 'label--small lg:label--base' %}
    {% endif %}
  </div>
  {% endif %}
</div>

{% comment %} ============ HALF-HORIZONTAL (800x240) ============ {% endcomment %}
{% when 'half-horizontal' %}
<div class="layout">
  <div class="flex flex--row gap--large flex--center-y grow">
    <div class="no-shrink">
      {% render 'card', card: hero, value_size: 'value--xxlarge lg:value--xxxlarge', label_size: 'label--base lg:label--large' %}
    </div>
    {% if my_count > 0 or all_count > 0 %}
    <div class="flex flex--col gap--small grow">
      {% if my_count > 0 %}
      {% render 'scope_group', heading: 'Me', scope_cards: my_cards, hero_key: hero_key, total_count: my_count, item_limit: 4, inner_class: 'grid grid--cols-5', value_size: 'value--small', label_size: 'label--small' %}
      {% endif %}
      {% if all_count > 0 %}
      {% render 'scope_group', heading: 'All', scope_cards: all_cards, hero_key: hero_key, total_count: all_count, item_limit: 4, inner_class: 'grid grid--cols-5', value_size: 'value--small', label_size: 'label--small' %}
      {% endif %}
    </div>
    {% endif %}
  </div>
</div>

{% comment %} ============= HALF-VERTICAL (400x480; 520x780 on TRMNL X) ============= {% endcomment %}
{% comment %} Body rows are one per metric type with both scopes, else the cards in pairs. Values are
the same CSS px on OG and TRMNL X, so each tier sets both, and sizes step down as rows grow so the
body fills the slot without overflowing. `flex` on the layout gives its `stretch` child a zero
min-height; without it the body grows past the slot instead of shrinking. {% endcomment %}
{% when 'half-vertical' %}
{% assign types = '' %}
{% for card in cards %}{% unless card.key == hero_key %}
{% assign t = card.key | remove_first: card.scope | remove_first: '_' %}
{% assign probe = ',' | append: types | append: ',' %}
{% assign needle = ',' | append: t | append: ',' %}
{% unless probe contains needle %}{% assign types = types | append: ',' | append: t %}{% endunless %}
{% endunless %}{% endfor %}
{% assign types = types | remove_first: ',' | split: ',' %}
{% if my_count > 0 and all_count > 0 %}
{% assign rows = types.size %}
{% else %}
{% assign rows = my_count | plus: all_count | plus: 1 | divided_by: 2 %}
{% endif %}
{% assign hero_label = 'label--base lg:label--large' %}
{% assign card_label = 'label--small lg:label--base' %}
{% if rows <= 3 %}
{% assign hero_size = 'value--xlarge lg:value--mega' %}{% assign card_size = 'value--base lg:value--xlarge' %}{% assign grid_gap = '' %}
{% elsif rows == 4 %}
{% assign hero_size = 'value--large lg:value--mega' %}{% assign card_size = 'value--small lg:value--large' %}{% assign grid_gap = 'gap--small lg:gap' %}
{% elsif rows == 5 %}
{% assign hero_size = 'value--large lg:value--xxxlarge' %}{% assign card_size = 'value--small lg:value--large' %}{% assign grid_gap = 'gap--small lg:gap' %}
{% else %}
{% assign hero_size = 'value--base lg:value--xxxlarge' %}{% assign hero_label = 'label--small lg:label--large' %}{% assign card_size = 'value--small lg:value--base' %}{% assign card_label = 'label--small' %}{% assign grid_gap = 'gap--xsmall lg:gap--small' %}
{% if rows > 6 %}{% assign hero_size = 'value--base lg:value--xxlarge' %}{% assign hero_label = 'label--small lg:label--base' %}{% endif %}
{% endif %}
<div class="layout layout--col flex">
  <div class="self--stretch">
    {% render 'card', card: hero, value_size: hero_size, label_size: hero_label %}
  </div>
  {% if my_count > 0 or all_count > 0 %}
  <div class="divider self--stretch"></div>
  {% if my_count > 0 and all_count > 0 %}
  {% render 'metric_rows', cards: cards, types: types, hero_key: hero_key, value_size: card_size, label_size: card_label, grid_gap: grid_gap %}
  {% elsif my_count > 0 %}
  {% render 'scope_grid', heading: 'Me', scope_cards: my_cards, hero_key: hero_key, value_size: card_size, label_size: card_label, grid_gap: grid_gap %}
  {% else %}
  {% render 'scope_grid', heading: 'All', scope_cards: all_cards, hero_key: hero_key, value_size: card_size, label_size: card_label, grid_gap: grid_gap %}
  {% endif %}
  {% endif %}
</div>

{% comment %} ============ QUADRANT (400x240, portrait 240x400) ============ {% endcomment %}
{% comment %} quadrant's two mounts have opposite orientations, 400x240 landscape and 240x400
portrait, so `portrait:flex--col` moves the hero from beside the scope groups to above them. A hero
on the left of the ~240px portrait frame squeezed the cards to ~60px ("Open"→"Oper"). Capped low
(`item_limit: 2`, `grid--cols-2`) so two stat cards per scope fit either way. {% endcomment %}
{% when 'quadrant' %}
<div class="layout">
  <div class="flex flex--row portrait:flex--col gap--small grow">
    <div class="no-shrink">
      {% render 'card', card: hero, value_size: 'value--xlarge lg:value--xxlarge', label_size: 'label--small lg:label--base' %}
    </div>
    {% if my_count > 0 or all_count > 0 %}
    <div class="flex flex--col gap--small grow self--stretch">
      {% if my_count > 0 %}
      {% render 'scope_group', heading: 'Me', scope_cards: my_cards, hero_key: hero_key, total_count: my_count, item_limit: 2, inner_class: 'grid grid--cols-2', value_size: 'value--small', label_size: 'label--small' %}
      {% endif %}
      {% if all_count > 0 %}
      {% render 'scope_group', heading: 'All', scope_cards: all_cards, hero_key: hero_key, total_count: all_count, item_limit: 2, inner_class: 'grid grid--cols-2', value_size: 'value--small', label_size: 'label--small' %}
      {% endif %}
    </div>
    {% endif %}
  </div>
</div>

{% endcase %}
{% endif %}

{% render 'title_bar', trmnl: trmnl, layout_size: layout_size, updated: updated %}

<script>
(function () {
  var locale = '{{ trmnl.user.locale }}' || undefined;
  var timeZone = '{{ trmnl.user.time_zone_iana }}' || undefined;
  var hour12 = {{ hour12 }};
  function formatter(opts) {
    opts.hour12 = hour12;
    try {
      return new Intl.DateTimeFormat(locale, Object.assign({ timeZone: timeZone }, opts));
    } catch (e) {
      {%- comment -%} Invalid locale or timezone: fall back to render-environment defaults {%- endcomment -%}
      return new Intl.DateTimeFormat(undefined, opts);
    }
  }
  var formats = {
    time: formatter({ hour: 'numeric', minute: '2-digit' })
  };
  document.querySelectorAll('[data-dt]').forEach(function (el) {
    var seconds = parseInt(el.getAttribute('data-dt'), 10);
    if (!seconds) return;
    var format = formats[el.getAttribute('data-dt-style')] || formats.time;
    el.textContent = format.format(new Date(seconds * 1000));
  });
})();
</script>
{% endtemplate %}
